& [ClosedSupport] is exact
  + supplied entry records assemble into a coherent but nonphysical metadata observation and incomplete topology seed
  + two supplied entry assemblies reconcile by exact ordered comparison while proving no time, handle, path, or Windows origin
  + regular-file supplied bytes derive a digest and bind to a newly revalidated stable pair through exact reference and length gates
  + regular-file placement joins the output-only content binding to caller-declared path, mode, and ordinal syntax
  + the completed regular-file projection preserves all lower evidence beside one current valid M2A observation in an output-only wrapper
  + global evidence is 332 passed with one governed physical ignore in debug and overflow-checked release

& [SupportDelta] exposes the next missing entry class
  + [closed] one complete lineage-preserving supplied regular-file structural carrier
  + [still_open] a complete lineage-preserving supplied directory structural carrier
  + [still_open] root-directory projection with its distinct null-path and root-binding semantics
  + [still_open] repeated mixed-entry inventory, duplicate identity and path detection, canonical ordering, and aggregate digest
  + [still_open] physical metadata and byte acquisition, common owned-handle provenance, actual pre-content-post order, and stream-query completion
  + [still_open] Git executable-mode truth, traversal-owned ordinal assignment, receipt production, and admission integration

& [ExistingFormMeaning] permits a directory-only composition
  + supplied assembly already derives a directory seed with directory kind, no length, policy-validated attributes, identity, link count, and an empty admitted stream set
  + supplied stability already accepts directory pairs and compares every field required by its structural profile
  + M2A already defines the directory shape as descendant path, directory mode, no length, and no content digest
  + directory projection needs no content-digest carrier and must not invent one
  + the publicly constructible and deserializable WindowsSuppliedEntryStablePair is not sufficient provenance input for a new output-only projection
  = therefore: the projection must consume WindowsSuppliedEntryStabilityInput and invoke the current reconciler internally before it may form success

& [CandidateComparison] is dependency ordered
  + [candidate_A] is implement the physical Windows producer
    - rejected because owned-handle provenance, initialized buffers, query completion, actual temporal order, and physical fixtures remain a larger unsafe-adjacent boundary
  + [candidate_B] is accept a WindowsSuppliedEntryStablePair directly
    - rejected because the type remains publicly constructible and deserializable; accepting it would permit forged success lineage
  + [candidate_C] is pure supplied directory topology projection with mandatory stability revalidation
    + consumes one strict directory placement plan and one complete supplied stability input
    + calls the current stability reconciler and rejects non-directory results
    + joins exact entry-reference identity and exact final path component
    + fixes mode to directory, omits length and content digest, maps only seed-supported facts, and calls current M2A validation
    + preserves the complete plan, revalidated stable pair, and topology form in a private Serialize-only wrapper
  + [candidate_D] is mixed-entry inventory reconciliation
    - deferred because directory and root projection carriers do not yet exist
  + [candidate_E] is root-directory projection
    - deferred because root null-path, canonical root identity, and preflight-root binding require a distinct contract rather than a descendant-component join
  + [candidate_F] is Git reconciliation, receipt, or admission
    - rejected because their evidence producers, repeated inventory, and physical provenance are not closed

& [SelectedBoundary] is pure supplied directory topology projection
  + [working_profile] is cantor-windows-supplied-directory-topology-projection/0.1
  + [plan] contains exact profile, nonzero projection identity, nonzero entry-reference identity, canonical descendant relative path, and nonzero caller-declared observation ordinal
  + [stability_input] is WindowsSuppliedEntryStabilityInput by value, never a bare stable pair or projection seed
  + [revalidation] calls reconcile_windows_supplied_entry_stability and nests the exact lower fault
  + [kind_gate] requires the revalidated pre-read seed to be Directory
  + [entry_reference_gate] requires exact plan and stable-pair equality
  + [component_gate] requires the final relative-path component to equal the stable policy component exactly
  + [projection] copies seed-supported attributes, identity, link count, and streams; fixes kind and mode to directory; omits length and digest; and copies path and ordinal only from the plan
  + [validation] applies the current ValidateTopologyForm implementation
  + [output] has private fields, Serialize only, immutable getters, and no public constructor, Default, Deserialize, or provenance-losing conversion
  + [Cargo_delta] is zero
  - never: accept a stable pair, bare observation, bare seed, asserted digest, or caller-selected mode as sufficient input
  - never: claim physical directory existence, path membership, enumeration, traversal order, stream completeness, Windows provenance, receipt, or admission

& [SemanticGrade] remains supplied structural projection
  + [derived] directory metadata is transformed only from revalidated supplied values
  + [declared] relative path, ordinal, projection identity, and entry-reference identity remain caller syntax
  + [correlated] means exact equality and structural relation under this profile only
  + [projected] means one valid M2A directory form nested beside its revalidated supplied lineage
  + [physical] remains absent
  + [admitted] remains absent

